**`(*sqlite.DB).CreateMemo`** — `store/db/sqlite/memo.go`; **traced the default driver config through the driver factory to the `store.Driver` dispatch, leaving only the SQLite implementation as the runtime candidate**

With no database flags, the default driver is SQLite:

```121:123:cmd/memos/main.go
	viper.SetDefault("demo", false)
	viper.SetDefault("driver", "sqlite")
	viper.SetDefault("port", 8081)
```

`profile.Validate()` also sets a SQLite DSN when none is provided (`internal/profile/profile.go:110-116`).

Startup wires that driver through the factory:

```18:20:store/db/db.go
	switch profile.Driver {
	case "sqlite":
		driver, err = sqlite.NewDB(profile)
```

Memo creation goes through the interface to whatever driver was constructed:

```109:113:store/memo.go
